  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "description": "This Red Hat security advisory addresses multiple vulnerabilities and bugs in the Linux kernel packages, which form the core of the operating system. The fixes cover a range of issues including memory corruption, out-of-bounds writes, use-after-free errors, buffer overflows, and privilege requirement enforcement across various kernel subsystems such as IPv6, DRM, netfilter, Bluetooth, and others. The advisory applies to Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 Extended Update Support and related builder products. A system reboot is required after applying the update to ensure the fixes take effect.",
